WEBVTT

00:06.506 --> 00:09.092
[opening theme song playing]

00:45.086 --> 00:47.505
[wistful music]

00:48.131 --> 00:50.675
You think I should live with you?

00:51.259 --> 00:52.218
Mm-hmm.

00:52.302 --> 00:53.970
It'd make me so happy.

00:55.847 --> 00:57.599
You could live here. Say you will.

01:02.395 --> 01:03.271
[inhales deeply]

01:04.355 --> 01:08.193
You sure it's a good idea?
It's not too fast for you?

01:11.362 --> 01:13.031
I can handle notifying everyone

01:13.114 --> 01:14.866
and returning all the gifts
we've received.

01:14.949 --> 01:17.243
But I'm keeping the honeymoon refund.
That's fair.

01:20.497 --> 01:24.292
We were together for ten years,
and I barely know you.

01:28.296 --> 01:29.798
[sighs]
What was it all for?

01:30.465 --> 01:32.884
It's such a long time
to spend with someone.

01:33.927 --> 01:37.722
Yet I never fully knew
if we really loved each other.

01:38.473 --> 01:41.559
[wistful music]

01:47.065 --> 01:49.400
It wasn't the right match and we knew it.

01:51.528 --> 01:54.781
I'm glad we figured it out
instead of waiting even longer.

01:55.740 --> 01:58.201
[soft chuckle]
That's true.

01:58.743 --> 02:02.122
It's kinda scary that it took us
ten years, though, right?

02:07.335 --> 02:09.337
[wistful music fading]

02:09.420 --> 02:12.173
I don't want to waste
another decade of my life.

02:14.384 --> 02:15.969
I want to get to know you,

02:16.594 --> 02:19.848
and find out if we're compatible
by living together.

02:20.807 --> 02:24.269
That way, it won't be long
until we know if we're gonna work.

02:24.853 --> 02:26.396
I should move in to get to know you?

02:26.479 --> 02:27.480
Mm-hmm.

02:28.314 --> 02:31.860
And since we agreed to lay low at work
since we have to be careful,

02:31.943 --> 02:35.780
doesn't it make sense for us
to optimize our time outside of work?

02:37.031 --> 02:39.701
Hmm, if it's honestly
just about efficiency,

02:40.285 --> 02:41.953
then I'm not down.

02:44.873 --> 02:46.040
You're not?

02:46.124 --> 02:47.584
I'm not.

02:49.085 --> 02:49.919
Why?

02:50.003 --> 02:54.507
First of all, I'm not taking such
a big step to "optimize" a relationship.

02:54.591 --> 02:57.719
There's a lot more to living together
than getting to know each other quickly.

02:58.344 --> 03:00.805
If it wasn't good, I'd wanna
talk about it, not call it off.

03:01.639 --> 03:05.602
So if it's just a big test,
then I won't move in with you for now.

03:07.145 --> 03:08.563
You don't even wanna try?

03:08.646 --> 03:11.024
'Cause I've done it before, moving in.

03:15.403 --> 03:18.114
[gloomy music]

03:18.197 --> 03:21.242
You have to tell me why.
We're not breaking up out of nowhere.

03:21.826 --> 03:23.828
- I got tired.
- Of what?

03:23.912 --> 03:25.163
Living like this.

03:25.246 --> 03:27.248
You're the reason why we live like this.

03:27.332 --> 03:30.043
- You said you wanted to.
- I did. You're not wrong.

03:30.543 --> 03:31.920
And it wasn't what I thought it'd be.

03:32.003 --> 03:34.505
It feels like we'll never fully grow up.

03:35.006 --> 03:36.716
And I want more from life than this.

03:38.426 --> 03:39.469
I'm sorry.

03:40.845 --> 03:42.222
[door lock chiming]

03:43.306 --> 03:44.307
[door slams]

03:45.558 --> 03:46.809
[door lock chiming]

03:49.145 --> 03:51.314
- [sighs]
- [thunder rumbles]

03:56.152 --> 03:58.154
[gloomy music]

04:00.615 --> 04:02.492
[Ki-jun] What do you mean hold off?

04:03.576 --> 04:05.119
Why would you want to put it off?

04:05.203 --> 04:06.120
Wait.

04:06.955 --> 04:08.081
Because of me?

04:08.164 --> 04:11.042
[breathes deeply]
I don't totally know.

04:11.709 --> 04:12.752
What?

04:13.336 --> 04:14.754
I just thought…

04:14.837 --> 04:17.006
when I got married,
I'd be happier with you.

04:18.383 --> 04:20.218
But right now, that doesn't seem true.

04:20.301 --> 04:22.971
We fight all the time
and you're always mad.

04:23.054 --> 04:25.974
Most days, you're a totally
different person from who I married.

04:26.599 --> 04:28.643
What changed, exactly? How am I different?

04:29.227 --> 04:30.270
You were ambitious.

04:31.437 --> 04:33.273
You were smart, but not full of yourself.

04:33.356 --> 04:35.108
And you were thoughtful and kind.

04:35.191 --> 04:37.944
But mostly, you were ambitious and…

04:38.695 --> 04:39.612
And now?

04:40.655 --> 04:41.614
I'm not any longer?

04:42.865 --> 04:44.742
You never wanna plan ahead.

04:49.414 --> 04:50.832
[sighs]

04:50.915 --> 04:54.085
Is this about needing a loan
to get our next place?

04:54.919 --> 04:56.004
[sighs]

04:56.713 --> 04:57.630
It is.

04:57.714 --> 05:00.466
[breathes deeply]

05:01.467 --> 05:05.305
If we register, make everything official,
and get the newlywed loan,

05:05.388 --> 05:06.681
what's the plan after that?

05:07.307 --> 05:10.935
Before we can finish off
paying the loan, rent is gonna go up.

05:11.019 --> 05:13.479
Then we'll need another loan
'cause we have to move again.

05:13.563 --> 05:14.939
Do we take out loans forever?

05:15.523 --> 05:17.775
We're both young.
We have plenty of time for that.

05:17.859 --> 05:19.986
What's the plan
when we're not young anymore?

05:20.570 --> 05:22.447
Ten years to pay back the first loan.

05:22.530 --> 05:24.574
And if we win the lottery
to own an apartment,

05:24.657 --> 05:28.036
that's 20 years paying a mortgage,
which is basically renting.

05:28.119 --> 05:30.330
And after that, we'll need
to think about retiring

05:30.413 --> 05:33.583
because I'm sure I don't still
wanna be working here when I'm old.

05:33.666 --> 05:35.710
That's just how it works, Yu-jin.

05:35.793 --> 05:37.545
Well, no one told me about that.

05:37.628 --> 05:38.755
[sighs]

05:41.340 --> 05:43.384
It took a lot to get to our wedding day.

05:43.468 --> 05:45.595
We worked so hard, it should be easier.

05:46.095 --> 05:49.682
Why does it feel like we're poor?
We work, but everything feels unstable.

05:52.268 --> 05:55.938
So did you think getting married
would make things easy?

05:56.898 --> 05:58.691
[sighs]

05:58.775 --> 05:59.901
No, I don't know.

06:01.277 --> 06:05.198
But I don't wanna register
until I figure out what we're doing.

06:07.408 --> 06:08.826
[exhales sharply]

06:14.957 --> 06:16.042
[sighs]

06:18.544 --> 06:20.338
[Ha-kyung] It seems so important.

06:20.963 --> 06:23.883
I probably wanted to avoid
making the same mistakes.

06:25.176 --> 06:29.722
I've never let someone get so close
as quickly as I wanted him to.

06:29.806 --> 06:32.934
I know you're trying
not to get hurt again.

06:34.352 --> 06:35.353
Yeah, that's right.

06:36.312 --> 06:37.563
I am, too.

06:38.773 --> 06:40.274
[Ha-kyung] But he says that

06:40.358 --> 06:44.403
if we get together too quickly,
we're more likely to be disappointed

06:44.487 --> 06:46.572
by little things that don't matter.

06:47.406 --> 06:49.450
And it would hurt even more
if we called it off.

06:50.785 --> 06:54.914
I know we want to open up,
but we need to protect ourselves too.

06:55.665 --> 06:56.666
[mug clanks]

06:57.542 --> 07:01.546
How do we compromise closeness?
What's the optimal distance?

07:01.629 --> 07:06.759
EPISODE 7
OZONE WARNING

07:06.843 --> 07:08.886
- [door lock chimes]
- [door opens]

07:11.264 --> 07:12.223
Oh…

07:13.808 --> 07:15.101
It's smaller than I thought.

07:15.184 --> 07:19.355
[realtor] Well, rent for this tiny thing
is at the very top of your budget.

07:19.439 --> 07:22.525
There's a waitlist for this place,
just to tour.

07:22.608 --> 07:24.110
I think we should keep looking.

07:24.193 --> 07:27.405
If this is too small, we should
really raise your budget.

07:27.488 --> 07:30.074
You'd be amazed at how much better
it gets if you go a little higher.

07:32.660 --> 07:35.079
Just let me know if there's
anything else at this price.

07:35.705 --> 07:37.081
O… kay.

07:37.165 --> 07:38.749
- [realtor chuckles]
- Thank you very much.

07:56.726 --> 07:57.727
[sighs]

08:18.456 --> 08:20.458
[pensive music]

08:25.671 --> 08:27.632
Stay out of trouble.
I'll be back real quick.

08:29.175 --> 08:30.384
[woman] You got one for me too?

08:31.594 --> 08:32.553
See you later.

08:35.431 --> 08:36.724
[door closes]

08:37.308 --> 08:38.518
[sighs]

08:46.108 --> 08:48.861
[somber music]

08:52.448 --> 08:53.866
[rain pouring]

09:05.962 --> 09:07.380
[man 1] Forty thousand.

09:08.130 --> 09:09.340
[man 2] Hey!

09:09.423 --> 09:11.551
[indistinct chatter, shouting]

09:11.634 --> 09:13.636
- [man 3] All right, all right.
- [man 4] All in.

09:13.719 --> 09:15.304
[men yelling]

09:15.388 --> 09:17.974
- [man 1] Yeah, come on!
- [man 2] I got it!

09:18.057 --> 09:20.268
[overlapping yells]

09:20.351 --> 09:22.562
- [man 3] Now, now.
- [man 4] I'll call. I'll call.

09:22.645 --> 09:24.355
[man 5] Let's see who's gonna take it.

09:24.438 --> 09:25.940
- [man 1] Oh, come on!
- [man 2] Come on!

09:26.023 --> 09:28.818
- [man 5] Let's see what you got.
- [man 1] Come on!

09:28.901 --> 09:30.820
- Two fives.
- Let's go. You're done!

09:30.903 --> 09:32.238
- I got two nines.
- Hey!

09:32.321 --> 09:33.990
[laughter]

09:35.324 --> 09:37.910
- Shut up and shuffle the cards.
- [laughter]

09:37.994 --> 09:39.870
[man 1] Okay, again. Just one drink.

09:39.954 --> 09:42.707
[man 2] Hey, shuffle already.
We ain't got all day.

09:42.790 --> 09:44.667
[man 3] Come on. Hurry up.

10:02.435 --> 10:05.688
DIRECTOR JIN HA-KYUNG

10:08.316 --> 10:11.444
[light music]

10:19.827 --> 10:23.289
["Something Precious" by Rothy playing]

10:33.966 --> 10:34.884
[page rustling]

10:57.114 --> 10:58.824
DIRECTOR JIN HA-KYUNG

11:11.796 --> 11:14.131
["Something Precious"
by Rothy continues playing]

11:33.734 --> 11:36.362
[music fading]

11:37.988 --> 11:40.366
INNOVATIVE WEATHER SERVICES
A STEPPING STONE TO PUBLIC SAFETY

11:40.449 --> 11:42.660
[birds chirping]

11:44.245 --> 11:46.080
[alarm ringing]

11:52.628 --> 11:54.255
[ringing continues]

11:56.132 --> 11:57.216
[Si-woo grunts]

11:57.299 --> 11:58.384
[alarm ringing]

12:00.761 --> 12:01.762
[Si-woo gasps]

12:07.059 --> 12:08.561
[exhales]

12:12.773 --> 12:13.983
[grunts]

12:15.359 --> 12:16.318
[groans]

12:30.583 --> 12:33.377
Excuse me. Do you have
any shampoo that I can use?

12:34.962 --> 12:36.172
Ah, thank you so much.

12:37.173 --> 12:39.425
[grunts]
Huh?

12:41.844 --> 12:44.597
MALE SHOWER ROOM

12:47.099 --> 12:48.100
[sighs]

12:53.314 --> 12:55.524
[quirky music]

13:00.988 --> 13:02.031
[door opens]

13:03.407 --> 13:05.201
NIGHT-DUTY ROOM

13:06.202 --> 13:07.286
[doorknob clanks]

13:10.247 --> 13:12.666
Man, he acts like he lives here
or something.

13:14.835 --> 13:16.003
- [Si-woo] Hello.
- Hey.

13:16.086 --> 13:19.673
[reporter] Some extremely hot sunlight
is telling us summer is finally here.

13:19.757 --> 13:23.928
UV levels will be very high
in those areas today.

13:24.011 --> 13:26.555
And ozone concentration
will be high as well.

13:26.639 --> 13:28.349
- [gasps]
- Don't forget to put on sunblock

13:28.432 --> 13:30.518
- before you go out…
- [Si-woo] Wow! This place is great.

13:34.188 --> 13:35.856
Is anyone using the top bunk?

13:36.941 --> 13:38.067
What are you saying?

13:38.734 --> 13:39.860
Are you scoping it out?

13:39.944 --> 13:41.779
How come you're staying
at the office in the first place?

13:42.363 --> 13:44.073
I have a good reason.

13:44.156 --> 13:45.699
Well, I do too.

13:47.952 --> 13:48.827
[grunts]

13:49.453 --> 13:52.206
Oh, I like this.
[chuckles]

13:53.249 --> 13:55.000
[Si-woo giggling]

13:58.295 --> 13:59.672
I'll be waiting out front.

14:00.589 --> 14:01.549
[Bo-mi] I'm coming.

14:02.091 --> 14:04.260
Hurry. I have so much to get done today.

14:04.343 --> 14:06.971
I'm going to have to swing by the office
for training this morning.

14:07.054 --> 14:08.597
Okay? And then, three open houses.

14:08.681 --> 14:09.807
So you'll be home late?

14:09.890 --> 14:11.642
You can have dinner for yourself.

14:11.725 --> 14:14.895
- There's rice in the rice cooker.
- And the sides are in the fridge.

14:14.979 --> 14:18.148
- I'll just take them out and eat.
- Oh, a little adult, aren't you?

14:20.150 --> 14:21.193
[clanks]

14:23.737 --> 14:24.947
[Bo-mi] Is it Dad's?

14:25.531 --> 14:26.866
[Hyang-rae] Why did he leave this?

14:26.949 --> 14:29.159
He does whatever he wants in the moment.

14:29.243 --> 14:31.537
I don't get why he'd come home,
then leave.

14:36.500 --> 14:39.545
Your Pop was never good
at throwing stuff away.

14:39.628 --> 14:40.629
[Hyang-rae chuckles]

14:40.713 --> 14:43.090
It's hard for me to get rid
of all these old things

14:43.173 --> 14:45.009
that he brings home here to me.

14:45.593 --> 14:46.844
Go ahead, if you want.

14:47.511 --> 14:48.429
Huh?

14:48.512 --> 14:49.805
Divorce.

14:50.639 --> 14:51.557
What?

14:51.640 --> 14:53.017
I'd survive it now.

14:56.103 --> 14:57.021
Bo-mi?

14:58.272 --> 14:59.940
You can't just say stuff like that.

15:00.441 --> 15:01.358
Bo-mi!

15:05.237 --> 15:06.947
- Bo-mi.
- [elevator dings]

15:07.031 --> 15:09.491
KOREA METEOROLOGICAL ADMINISTRATION

15:11.327 --> 15:13.871
- You're here early.
- Why were you in there?

15:14.580 --> 15:17.499
Uh… I had something to do.

15:17.583 --> 15:18.584
Hmm.

15:23.172 --> 15:24.173
And yesterday?

15:24.256 --> 15:26.050
I had some things to take care of.

15:27.468 --> 15:28.427
Why?

15:29.011 --> 15:32.598
Oh, I was just wondering
because you didn't call or…

15:34.683 --> 15:36.101
You were waiting for a call?

15:36.852 --> 15:37.686
[scoffs]
No.

15:38.604 --> 15:39.730
You were, though.

15:39.813 --> 15:41.148
No, I was not, really.

15:43.359 --> 15:45.736
[playful music]

15:50.032 --> 15:51.617
What are you doing? We're at work.

15:53.243 --> 15:54.453
You were waiting.

15:54.536 --> 15:56.121
I could see it on your face.

15:56.205 --> 15:57.081
[laughs]

15:58.082 --> 16:00.209
I guess you haven't heard, Forecaster.

16:00.292 --> 16:02.962
I'm kinda famous in the KMA
for my poker face.

16:03.045 --> 16:04.213
Also, how do they say it?

16:04.296 --> 16:06.590
I was born to put up walls
or something like that.

16:06.674 --> 16:08.884
- Who said that?
- I did.

16:08.968 --> 16:11.720
You've got a gift
for self-analysis, really.

16:13.097 --> 16:15.099
You're getting too familiar, okay?

16:15.182 --> 16:17.559
Just, um, professional friendliness.

16:18.060 --> 16:19.603
I don't know why a forecaster

16:19.687 --> 16:21.397
would need to be friendly
with his director.

16:21.480 --> 16:23.482
- Well, we're special.
- What's so--

16:24.066 --> 16:25.234
Good morning.

16:25.317 --> 16:27.111
- Good morning!
- Hello, Assistant Director.

16:33.409 --> 16:34.368
[softly]
Let's go.

16:38.372 --> 16:39.790
Hello, and good morning.

16:44.712 --> 16:46.630
KOREA METEOROLOGICAL ADMINISTRATION

16:48.590 --> 16:50.092
- [automated voice] Doors closing.
- Oh, wait, hold the door.

16:50.175 --> 16:52.261
Please hold the door. Please.
Please. Thanks.

16:53.345 --> 16:54.304
Hello.

16:54.388 --> 16:56.223
Oh, um, thank you.

16:57.224 --> 16:58.517
[automated voice] Doors closing.

17:01.061 --> 17:04.314
I saw your husband register
for leave of absence?

17:05.274 --> 17:09.319
Oh, when I was in Disaster Prevention,
he was my advisor.

17:09.403 --> 17:11.488
Ah.
[chuckles]

17:11.572 --> 17:13.699
He's not unwell or anything, is he?

17:13.782 --> 17:15.159
Ah, nothing like that.

17:15.242 --> 17:18.412
He wants to study for something,
so I said he should take a year off.

17:18.495 --> 17:19.872
What about your household?

17:19.955 --> 17:21.373
[chuckles]
Well, I've got it.

17:21.957 --> 17:23.125
Oh, wow.

17:23.208 --> 17:25.461
Isn't your younger son
just starting elementary school?

17:25.544 --> 17:27.254
Won't it be hard if you're the only…

17:27.838 --> 17:31.550
Well, we're married
and we both are there for the other.

17:31.633 --> 17:33.010
[automated voice] Doors opening.

17:37.848 --> 17:39.183
[Myung-ju] Isn't this your floor?

17:42.478 --> 17:43.854
[automated voice] Doors closing.

17:51.653 --> 17:53.614
- [exhales]
- Oh, thanks.

17:54.114 --> 17:55.365
[Ki-jun] Here you go.

17:57.576 --> 18:00.245
[Ki-jun chuckles, clears throat]

18:00.329 --> 18:02.247
Is something going on?

18:02.831 --> 18:04.041
Oh, the thing is…

18:04.541 --> 18:06.960
I have a friend
who got married not long ago.

18:08.128 --> 18:09.171
Ah.
[awkward chuckle]

18:11.632 --> 18:12.591
Okay, so?

18:12.674 --> 18:13.884
He did the whole wedding

18:13.967 --> 18:18.138
even though everyone told him not to
'cause he was sure he loved her.

18:18.222 --> 18:19.098
Okay.

18:19.181 --> 18:20.265
So they had their wedding,

18:20.349 --> 18:23.268
saw the whole thing through,
and now they won't agree to register it.

18:24.061 --> 18:25.646
Your friend or his wife?

18:25.729 --> 18:27.189
Wife, of course.

18:27.272 --> 18:28.732
What do you think she's thinking?

18:28.816 --> 18:31.151
[gasps]
Oh, well…

18:31.652 --> 18:33.403
I do understand.

18:34.613 --> 18:36.115
You understand her?

18:36.198 --> 18:37.366
Mm-hmm.

18:37.449 --> 18:40.244
She could have conceivably jumped
into this wedding out of impulse.

18:40.327 --> 18:43.831
However, ultimately,
when it finally came to register,

18:44.832 --> 18:46.875
she finally started to see things clearly.

18:48.085 --> 18:49.086
Oh.

18:49.878 --> 18:53.215
Then, is she regretting doing it now?

18:53.298 --> 18:54.716
Or it could be…

18:55.300 --> 18:56.677
she suddenly was scared.

18:56.760 --> 18:57.970
Hmm?

18:59.513 --> 19:02.516
I think, sometimes,
when it's not just the heart,

19:02.599 --> 19:05.978
but actually the law,
it feels like you're crossing a line

19:06.061 --> 19:08.939
where you can never again
go back to the other side.

19:09.022 --> 19:11.608
[breathing deeply]

19:11.692 --> 19:12.693
[exhales deeply]

19:13.402 --> 19:15.154
Possibly this wife of his

19:15.821 --> 19:18.532
is unsure about the marriage
in the first place.

19:19.032 --> 19:20.742
Love is trusting together.

19:22.202 --> 19:25.956
They say that where there's trust,
courage will appear also.

19:26.790 --> 19:31.003
The courage to go through anything
if it's along with the one you love, okay?

19:35.465 --> 19:37.467
[pensive music]

19:44.057 --> 19:47.186
- [Ha-kyung] How is the atmosphere?
- [Dong-han] Hmm, the upper level trough

19:47.269 --> 19:48.812
is slowly moving on to the East Sea,

19:48.896 --> 19:52.399
so the flow of the anticyclone of Korea
is going to be slow for a while.

19:52.482 --> 19:54.151
And solar radiation's going up.

19:55.110 --> 19:57.196
And the concentration
of ozone will rise as well.

19:57.905 --> 20:01.325
It might get all the way
to the warning level by noon.

20:01.992 --> 20:05.996
Oh, great. The phones are all
gonna start ringing off the hook today.

20:06.622 --> 20:08.248
Call to the Air Quality
Forecasting Center.

20:08.332 --> 20:09.458
Sure.

20:10.459 --> 20:14.504
NATIONAL METEOROLOGICAL CENTER
COMPREHENSIVE CONTROL SYSTEM

20:17.799 --> 20:19.343
[phone clanks]

20:21.845 --> 20:23.847
[light music]

20:25.349 --> 20:26.975
It's ironic, isn't it?

20:27.059 --> 20:28.227
Hmm? What?

20:29.311 --> 20:30.395
Ozone, I mean.

20:31.355 --> 20:34.775
It's really helpful
when it's in the stratosphere.

20:35.817 --> 20:38.278
But it's a hazard when it gets too close.

20:39.321 --> 20:40.155
[tongue clicks]

20:40.239 --> 20:42.824
Well, there's an optimal distance
for everything.

20:43.575 --> 20:45.702
At least we can calculate
the ideal distance

20:45.786 --> 20:47.537
between ozone and humans.

20:48.288 --> 20:50.999
Other boundaries
are impossible to figure out.

20:51.583 --> 20:52.918
Oh? What, for example?

20:53.001 --> 20:55.420
Like for two people, you know, it's…

20:55.504 --> 20:56.922
[laughs]

20:57.547 --> 21:00.259
There's no way of knowing
until you just confront it.

21:00.759 --> 21:01.885
[chuckles]

21:02.469 --> 21:06.348
I heard once that hedgehogs
poke each other a thousand times

21:06.431 --> 21:09.351
before they figure out how close
they can get without hurting each other.

21:10.727 --> 21:12.062
You can't avoid hurting each other

21:12.145 --> 21:15.065
in the process of figuring out
how close you can get.

21:15.148 --> 21:16.191
[Dong-han] That's right.

21:17.234 --> 21:21.863
Well, there's people who have been trying
to work it out for over a decade.

21:22.447 --> 21:23.323
Like I am.

21:26.618 --> 21:28.036
Did you go back home?

21:29.079 --> 21:30.038
No.

21:30.122 --> 21:32.124
I was away too long, I think.

21:32.708 --> 21:37.754
And now, the optimal distance
between me and my family is pretty far.

21:38.297 --> 21:40.632
Maybe it's best to just see them
once in a while,

21:41.258 --> 21:43.760
the way we're doing it right now.

21:44.261 --> 21:46.638
Oh, no. That's a poor excuse.

21:47.222 --> 21:48.265
You think so?

21:50.309 --> 21:51.518
[chuckles]

21:55.397 --> 21:57.524
The rainfall probability
is low today, right?

21:59.318 --> 22:02.112
Right. It's lower than 20 percent.

22:02.821 --> 22:04.489
Okay. Mm, thanks.

22:05.240 --> 22:10.954
Everyone, today we can expect to have
over a 0.3ppm ozone concentration.

22:11.538 --> 22:14.124
The Air Quality Forecasting Center
will keep calling us

22:14.207 --> 22:17.419
to check on solar radiation
and cloud coverage, so be cooperative.

22:17.502 --> 22:21.381
Please respond quickly and politely
to ozone situation increase, all right?

22:21.465 --> 22:22.758
- Yes, ma'am.
- Yes, ma'am.

22:23.425 --> 22:25.093
- [keyboard clacking]
- [mouse clicking]

22:25.177 --> 22:26.386
I can't do that.

22:26.470 --> 22:27.679
You know dealing with the press

22:27.763 --> 22:30.015
is already more than enough work
during monsoon season.

22:30.599 --> 22:32.350
Plus, I'm writing a column every month.

22:32.434 --> 22:34.019
How can I write a feature article too?

22:34.102 --> 22:37.689
I'm aware. That's why I told him
that it might not happen.

22:38.315 --> 22:41.276
But I do think they're gonna bug
Reporter Chae about this.

22:41.359 --> 22:42.944
I'm talking about your wife.

22:43.028 --> 22:44.112
Sorry?

22:44.196 --> 22:46.823
Their chief editor
asked for you specifically.

22:47.449 --> 22:50.952
They asked if Deputy Director Han Ki-jun
was Chae Yu-jin's husband.

22:54.331 --> 22:56.917
Let's just see what's…
what's really going on here.

22:57.000 --> 22:58.293
[exhales softly]

22:58.960 --> 22:59.878
Huh?

23:00.629 --> 23:01.880
A feature article?

23:02.839 --> 23:05.967
Isn't your husband a spokesman at the KMA?

23:06.051 --> 23:08.512
The guy on TV
whenever there's a weather alert.

23:10.263 --> 23:11.306
Yeah.

23:11.389 --> 23:12.933
And he's such a great writer.

23:13.517 --> 23:16.812
I always read his magazine column.
"Ozone High and Low."

23:16.895 --> 23:19.064
Right? That's your husband?

23:19.147 --> 23:20.649
[awkward chuckle]

23:20.732 --> 23:21.900
Yes.

23:21.983 --> 23:24.319
Could you ask him to use that talent

23:24.402 --> 23:26.238
to write us a new feature article
on weather?

23:27.364 --> 23:29.658
- [editor] Okay?
- Oh…

23:31.034 --> 23:34.079
[phone ringing]

23:34.621 --> 23:37.124
KI-JUN

23:39.876 --> 23:41.628
[phone vibrates]

23:42.170 --> 23:44.131
KI-JUN

23:44.714 --> 23:46.508
[phone vibrates]

23:52.639 --> 23:54.141
Oppa, what's going on?

23:54.224 --> 23:57.269
- Hey, you busy?
- [Yu-jin] No, not really.

23:57.853 --> 24:00.188
Why? Why are you calling?

24:00.272 --> 24:02.566
Well, I don't need a reason to call you.

24:02.649 --> 24:04.776
I just wanted to hear your sweet voice.

24:06.945 --> 24:07.863
So everything's good?

24:09.531 --> 24:11.783
[somber music]

24:13.910 --> 24:17.372
Yeah. Of… of course, yeah.

24:17.455 --> 24:19.040
Ah, I see.

24:20.458 --> 24:21.543
Okay, then.

24:22.252 --> 24:24.004
You can go back to work.
I'll see you at home.

24:24.087 --> 24:26.256
Oh, uh, okay.

24:30.510 --> 24:31.636
[sighs]

24:39.603 --> 24:40.854
[ringing]

24:42.063 --> 24:44.900
- Kim Soo-jin from Team Two here.
- Is this the weather authority?

24:44.983 --> 24:47.819
How can you slap us
with an ozone warning out of nowhere?

24:48.445 --> 24:50.155
My preschooler's got a field trip today.

24:50.238 --> 24:52.908
I took a whole day off of work
to chaperone for her.

24:53.617 --> 24:55.869
I mean, you should at least
give us one day of warning.

24:55.952 --> 24:58.914
Of course. Ozone levels
can increase very suddenly

24:58.997 --> 25:00.957
because of car exhausts
and other air pollutants.

25:01.041 --> 25:03.168
The warnings go out as soon as we know.

25:03.251 --> 25:06.546
Also, we're not the ones
who send the alert to the public.

25:06.630 --> 25:08.381
Don't be ridiculous. Hey!

25:08.465 --> 25:11.384
[trucker] The weather is perfectly fine.
What's with the ozone warning?

25:11.468 --> 25:12.969
They're telling all of us, truckers,

25:13.053 --> 25:15.764
that our cargo trucks won't be allowed
into the metro area.

25:15.847 --> 25:17.515
Are you gonna pay for our delays?

25:17.599 --> 25:21.144
Okay, listen, sir. There's never
a good reason to be rude.

25:21.228 --> 25:24.105
Talk to the Environmental Ministry
or the Road Authority about it.

25:24.189 --> 25:27.067
Our office is not responsible
for the actual warning.

25:27.150 --> 25:29.319
But isn't ozone a good thing, though?

25:29.402 --> 25:31.112
Something like we need an ozone layer.

25:31.196 --> 25:33.448
Yes, that's right,
when it's in the stratosphere.

25:33.531 --> 25:36.493
It's harmful to the human body
when there's too much near the surface.

25:36.576 --> 25:39.079
Oh, I see. Hmm.

25:39.162 --> 25:44.376
By the way, how old are you, miss?
You sound cute. You single?

25:45.252 --> 25:46.419
[sighs]
Goodbye.

25:46.962 --> 25:47.796
[phone clanks]

25:48.672 --> 25:50.799
- [phone ringing]
- [sighs]

25:52.384 --> 25:53.551
[exhales sharply]

25:53.635 --> 25:54.552
[ringing continues]

25:55.053 --> 25:57.138
I can get it. Go and get some food.

25:57.222 --> 25:59.057
I got them. I'm really okay.

25:59.140 --> 26:00.475
You can do this later.

26:01.101 --> 26:03.186
- I'm not hungry.
- [phone clanks]

26:04.104 --> 26:06.398
Hello, this is Kim Soo-jin with Team Two.

26:08.066 --> 26:11.778
Yes. But ozone warnings
are not the KMA's responsibility.

26:11.861 --> 26:13.822
Oh, hello, sir.

26:13.905 --> 26:15.323
- [Bong-chan] Hey.
- Hello.

26:15.407 --> 26:16.283
Hmm.

26:17.117 --> 26:18.118
Where is Director Jin?

26:18.201 --> 26:21.162
Uh, Policy Division
to talk about the post-analysis.

26:21.246 --> 26:22.247
Oh, I see.

26:22.914 --> 26:24.916
- Uh, carry on. Carry on.
- Yes, sir.

26:27.252 --> 26:28.295
Keep it up.

26:29.462 --> 26:31.047
- Oh, Mr. Um.
- Yes?

26:32.007 --> 26:34.092
Let's grab a coffee. Come on.

26:37.429 --> 26:38.388
[clears throat]

26:43.727 --> 26:44.602
Sir, please.

26:44.686 --> 26:46.104
Please just stop shouting.

26:46.604 --> 26:48.773
[man yelling]
What? Shouting?

26:49.274 --> 26:51.526
I think you're confused. I did not shout.

26:51.609 --> 26:52.694
You did, sir.

26:52.777 --> 26:55.405
You've been shouting at me
ever since we started our call.

26:55.905 --> 26:57.574
Why you… Hey!

26:57.657 --> 27:00.702
Do you want to get suspended?
Who do you think you're talking to?

27:00.785 --> 27:02.996
[man] I could make you write me
an apology letter.

27:03.079 --> 27:04.748
- [exhales sharply]
- Hey!

27:04.831 --> 27:06.958
My son is a high-ranking public official.

27:07.042 --> 27:10.378
One word to him and your career is over.
You get me, sweetheart?

27:11.629 --> 27:12.714
Good afternoon, sir.

27:12.797 --> 27:14.883
If your son's so great, maybe you can go

27:14.966 --> 27:18.511
and complain about the weather to him
instead of just calling us about it.

27:19.095 --> 27:22.474
[Myung-ju] Also, ozone warnings
are not under the KMA's jurisdiction.

27:22.557 --> 27:26.019
They're the Ministry of Environment's.
How can we make that more clear?

27:26.102 --> 27:29.522
If you wanna yell at someone,
yell at them. I don't care. Good day!

27:29.606 --> 27:32.275
- [phone slams]
- [exhales sharply]

27:32.359 --> 27:34.319
[tense music]

27:41.451 --> 27:42.911
Can we do that?

27:43.495 --> 27:45.747
No, we can't… But…

27:47.165 --> 27:48.416
we're human beings.

27:49.501 --> 27:52.837
We have the right to defend ourselves
if abuse is thrown at us.

27:52.921 --> 27:54.005
I don't know.

27:55.965 --> 27:58.968
It's fine, Ms. Kim. Don't worry.

27:59.052 --> 28:00.512
I'll handle the fallout.

28:11.648 --> 28:12.857
[vibrates]

28:25.537 --> 28:27.414
[Ha-kyung] Oh, where
are you going, Forecaster?

28:27.497 --> 28:30.708
- Oh, I have something to take care of.
- [phone vibrates]

28:30.792 --> 28:33.795
- See you.
- [vibrating continues]

28:36.673 --> 28:38.091
[clinking]

28:39.926 --> 28:40.885
Sorry?

28:41.511 --> 28:42.971
Ten mil and 600K?

28:44.305 --> 28:45.890
And maintenance expenses too?

28:47.475 --> 28:48.601
Um…

28:49.686 --> 28:53.648
What about 500,000
including the maintenance costs?

28:53.732 --> 28:55.525
I told you I can't do that.

28:55.608 --> 28:58.194
For 500,000, the place
you saw yesterday was the best option.

28:58.278 --> 29:01.322
Could you ask the building owner
about it just once more?

29:01.406 --> 29:03.408
I'm a very, very good tenant.

29:03.491 --> 29:05.952
And I'll basically only be there
to sleep, no more.

29:06.035 --> 29:08.538
I mean, we already know
what their answer is.

29:09.414 --> 29:11.666
I would really appreciate it
so much, ma'am.

29:11.750 --> 29:12.834
Thank you.

29:15.003 --> 29:16.504
[Bong-chan] Yes, I understand.

29:18.214 --> 29:19.799
- I'm aware of the situation.
- [sighs]

29:22.427 --> 29:25.889
Did you come all the way to Headquarters
just to act like some sad widower?

29:26.389 --> 29:27.640
[Dong-han] What are you talking about?

29:27.724 --> 29:30.643
I'm not a widower.
I have my wife and my daughter.

29:31.728 --> 29:34.731
[Bong-chan] I know you do.
You have a home, a wife, and a kid.

29:34.814 --> 29:37.317
So why are you crashing here for free
like you're homeless?

29:38.234 --> 29:40.111
The weather alerts are serious right now.

29:40.195 --> 29:42.530
Back in the day, we used
to almost live in the building

29:42.614 --> 29:44.532
during the worst of the monsoon season.

29:44.616 --> 29:45.658
So, uh, what's wrong?

29:45.742 --> 29:48.828
That's right. That was when we
didn't have a central server here, man.

29:50.038 --> 29:51.414
Why would you need to do that now

29:51.498 --> 29:54.042
when you could be in bed and look
at the charts all the way to China?

29:54.876 --> 29:55.877
Anyway…

29:56.377 --> 29:58.171
- [Dong-han sighs]
- All the young people

29:58.254 --> 29:59.839
hate that you're doing this.

29:59.923 --> 30:02.008
What do you mean by "the young people"?

30:02.550 --> 30:05.136
Lots of them wanna use
the night-duty room sometimes.

30:05.720 --> 30:08.640
They all think it's weird
that you're basically living in there.

30:08.723 --> 30:11.851
I got a whole stack
of complaints this high, okay?

30:11.935 --> 30:14.437
[smacks lips, groans]
Uh-huh.

30:15.480 --> 30:17.357
Pack up and get your stuff out of there.

30:18.441 --> 30:21.569
You took a pay cut to come to Headquarters
so you could be closer to your family.

30:22.153 --> 30:23.530
That's the only reason you're here.

30:23.613 --> 30:26.366
You could have just stayed
at the top of the Gangwon Office,

30:26.449 --> 30:28.243
- and you'd have been set.
- Ah, people in Seoul

30:28.326 --> 30:29.994
are too cold-hearted for me, okay?

30:30.078 --> 30:32.956
Does your wife know
that you're just moping around over here?

30:34.582 --> 30:36.960
She told me to do whatever I want.

30:41.548 --> 30:42.423
Well, you do that.

30:43.174 --> 30:44.259
[Bong-chan sucks teeth]

30:44.342 --> 30:47.971
A talent for knowing the winds
of the east wind is no good if, uh…

30:48.513 --> 30:50.431
if you can't even get a read
on your own wife.

30:51.015 --> 30:51.933
Here, toss this for me.

30:57.856 --> 30:58.898
[sighs]

31:00.024 --> 31:02.026
[gentle music]

31:03.695 --> 31:05.029
[sighs]

31:08.700 --> 31:11.160
[birds chirping]

31:13.288 --> 31:15.498
[tense music]

31:16.749 --> 31:18.543
[Ki-jun] Who was handling
the complaint calls

31:18.626 --> 31:20.086
that came in to Team Two today?

31:20.879 --> 31:22.046
I was.

31:23.756 --> 31:24.757
[Ha-kyung] What's this about?

31:25.341 --> 31:27.343
Your Bureau has received
a conduct warning.

31:28.970 --> 31:31.681
I heard you scolded someone
who called out the ozone warning

31:31.764 --> 31:34.434
for asking about things
outside KMA jurisdiction.

31:36.603 --> 31:39.022
Believe me. I know it's hard
to deal with complaint calls,

31:39.105 --> 31:41.232
but you can't just tell them off
and then hang up.

31:43.401 --> 31:45.320
Is this the truth, Ms. Kim?

31:46.446 --> 31:47.780
Um, uh…

31:47.864 --> 31:48.823
I did it.

31:50.491 --> 31:52.827
This is not the time
to cover for her, Assistant Director.

31:52.911 --> 31:54.287
I'm not covering anything.

31:54.370 --> 31:55.914
I took the call.

31:57.457 --> 31:58.583
Look what happens.

31:59.083 --> 32:01.169
Take responsibility
for your own failings, and look.

32:01.252 --> 32:03.630
Is this something that she
should have to take the blame for?

32:03.713 --> 32:05.757
What are you saying, Deputy Director Han?

32:05.840 --> 32:09.677
I took the call. I was on the call.
I yelled at the caller.

32:09.761 --> 32:11.721
It wasn't her. Are we clear?

32:15.099 --> 32:16.893
You should have restrained yourself.

32:16.976 --> 32:18.144
That was not an option.

32:18.227 --> 32:19.854
He was bragging he can get us all fired.

32:19.938 --> 32:21.397
What am I supposed to say to that?

32:21.898 --> 32:24.484
That's not a complaint, sir.
That's abusive.

32:24.567 --> 32:27.570
We're not some kind of trash can
they can just throw their anger in.

32:27.654 --> 32:30.990
We don't have to just sit there
and deal with that kind of crap.

32:33.034 --> 32:34.160
All right, then.

32:35.078 --> 32:38.289
Anyway, try to do a better job, Ms. Kim.

32:40.333 --> 32:42.919
Why would you let Mrs. Oh
take your calls and create this mess?

32:43.002 --> 32:45.755
This whole thing went down
'cause you couldn't handle your job.

32:45.838 --> 32:46.798
Wouldn't you say?

32:46.881 --> 32:48.633
Deputy Director Han, that's enough.

32:48.716 --> 32:50.301
[Soo-jin] It's all too much to take.

32:50.385 --> 32:51.552
[Soo-jin sniffles]

32:52.553 --> 32:54.138
What was I supposed to do

32:54.222 --> 32:56.724
when the first thing he said was,
"Do you know who my son is?"

32:57.558 --> 32:58.851
That's not all.

32:58.935 --> 33:00.520
Every one of these people is so rude.

33:00.603 --> 33:02.772
They all ask this weird stuff
like if I'm married.

33:02.855 --> 33:04.774
Plus they say I'm a dumb brat.

33:05.817 --> 33:06.776
[sniffles]

33:08.528 --> 33:10.863
- [Soo-jin cries]
- Uh…

33:10.947 --> 33:15.159
I'm here at the KMA
because I wanted to forecast weather.

33:15.243 --> 33:17.120
I didn't do all that work in school

33:17.203 --> 33:19.330
only to come here
and work in a call center.

33:25.420 --> 33:26.921
- [Soo-jin whimpers]
- Do-don't…

33:27.005 --> 33:30.591
I'll write a report on this,
following the proper procedure.

33:31.300 --> 33:32.260
You can go now.

33:32.343 --> 33:33.928
Oh, uh, um…

33:34.512 --> 33:36.180
Uh, all right.

33:46.107 --> 33:47.692
[door opens]

33:52.947 --> 33:54.198
Ms. Kim.

33:54.782 --> 33:55.742
Yes?

33:56.617 --> 33:58.995
We are here to do that kind of work.

34:03.082 --> 34:05.168
What are you saying right now, Director?

34:07.170 --> 34:13.217
I know it's hard to listen
to the callers and their… complaints.

34:13.301 --> 34:19.390
It's crazy to see how many people's lives
are affected by some… ozone warning, huh?

34:23.144 --> 34:25.605
Cargo truck drivers
whose lives are at stake,

34:25.688 --> 34:27.190
children who can't play outside,

34:27.273 --> 34:30.109
and people who don't even know
what ozone warnings mean.

34:30.193 --> 34:34.072
If we didn't have to hear out
every one of these people's complaints,

34:34.155 --> 34:36.157
could we have known, hmm?

34:38.284 --> 34:39.660
Could we have understood

34:39.744 --> 34:42.914
who our forecasts affect
and the ways they're affected?

34:46.501 --> 34:49.003
We all studied hard to pass
the civil service exam

34:49.087 --> 34:50.338
and be where we are right now.

34:50.922 --> 34:53.382
So we can serve the people
and protect them too.

34:54.967 --> 34:58.638
So listen. We're not just a call center.

34:58.721 --> 35:00.515
Our jobs here are crucial.

35:00.598 --> 35:01.682
Do you understand?

35:02.433 --> 35:03.434
[sniffles]

35:03.518 --> 35:06.395
[somber music]

35:15.696 --> 35:16.739
Are you okay?

35:16.823 --> 35:18.241
[light tapping]

35:19.408 --> 35:20.618
[Myung-ju] You did good.

35:27.542 --> 35:28.626
[phone clanks]

35:29.919 --> 35:33.631
I didn't study hard
to pass the civil service exam

35:33.714 --> 35:36.717
just so I could sit here
and take calls from rude strangers.

35:36.801 --> 35:39.512
Why do I have to put up
with this kind of treatment now?

35:42.014 --> 35:45.893
Why do you think we're all here
after all of our studying?

35:48.062 --> 35:51.065
It's so we can serve the public interest.

35:51.149 --> 35:53.818
To make sure we do our best every day.

35:53.901 --> 35:55.903
That's why the taxpayers pay our salaries.

35:55.987 --> 35:58.197
You thought this was some easy stable job?

35:58.281 --> 35:59.407
Well, it isn't.

35:59.490 --> 36:02.368
You should find a new line of work,
if that's what you're after.

36:02.451 --> 36:06.038
You can't work here if you don't have
a sense of duty and responsibility.

36:06.122 --> 36:07.081
Understand?

36:09.292 --> 36:10.209
Yes, sir.

36:14.589 --> 36:15.882
[light chuckle]

36:21.095 --> 36:22.638
She's grown, huh?

36:25.641 --> 36:26.726
Cheer up.

36:26.809 --> 36:30.229
I'm sorry that you got scolded
for something I did, too.

36:31.147 --> 36:32.982
Well, it didn't feel like a scolding.

36:33.900 --> 36:36.694
It actually hit me square in the skull.

36:38.946 --> 36:41.490
While I was answering phone calls
from rude people all day long,

36:41.574 --> 36:44.368
I thought, "What's my real purpose here?"

36:44.952 --> 36:48.664
But what Director Jin said to me
showed me purpose.

36:48.748 --> 36:50.666
Are you serious?
[gasps]

36:50.750 --> 36:53.085
Our Kim Soo-jin's all grown up now.
[chuckling]

36:53.169 --> 36:54.128
[giggles]

36:54.212 --> 36:55.963
[Dong-han] These are the moments
where you grow as a person.

36:56.047 --> 36:59.842
Even Jin Ha-kyung
wasn't born like that, right?

36:59.926 --> 37:02.303
[tongue clicks]
Anyway, see you.

37:02.386 --> 37:03.930
- See you all later, okay?
- [Myung-ju] Oh.

37:04.013 --> 37:05.014
- Goodbye.
- Good night, sir.

37:05.097 --> 37:06.432
Good night. See you.

37:09.435 --> 37:11.854
I guess he's going to sleep
down there again.

37:12.647 --> 37:14.065
He was away for too long.

37:14.148 --> 37:16.525
- Home can be difficult for him.
- [elevator dings]

37:17.109 --> 37:18.486
[automated voice] Doors opening.

37:18.569 --> 37:19.654
Hello.

37:19.737 --> 37:20.780
- Hello.
- Hello.

37:23.115 --> 37:24.242
You're going?

37:24.325 --> 37:26.369
Oh, go ahead, really.
I'm gonna take the next one down.

37:27.245 --> 37:28.955
- See you tomorrow, Forecaster.
- Good night.

37:29.038 --> 37:30.373
[automated voice] Doors closing.

37:31.916 --> 37:33.292
[automated voice] Doors opening.

37:35.127 --> 37:38.130
[sighs]
Oh, please go ahead.

37:38.214 --> 37:39.840
- Okay.
- [Si-woo] Yeah.

37:40.341 --> 37:41.676
[button clicks]

37:41.759 --> 37:43.094
[automated voice] Doors closing.

37:44.262 --> 37:47.014
[pensive music]

37:53.437 --> 37:55.940
- [elevator dings]
- [automated voice] Doors opening.

38:00.486 --> 38:01.737
Oh, please go ahead.

38:01.821 --> 38:03.364
- [automated voice] Doors closing.
- Bye.

38:06.325 --> 38:07.576
[clicks]

38:09.036 --> 38:11.497
[light upbeat music]

38:14.500 --> 38:15.668
[sighs]

38:41.152 --> 38:42.570
What are you doing here?

38:42.653 --> 38:46.324
Oh, the elevator was full.
So I was waiting for the next one.

38:46.407 --> 38:47.283
Mm.

38:48.159 --> 38:50.369
I'm hungry. Wanna get food now?

38:52.997 --> 38:54.165
Naengsam?

38:54.248 --> 38:55.166
Sure.

38:56.083 --> 38:57.835
CHILDREN'S BOOKS
BEST SELLERS AND NEW RELEASES

39:12.099 --> 39:14.143
Is this the book
that you were looking for?

39:14.226 --> 39:15.770
- Yes, it is. Thank you.
- [woman chuckles]

39:16.312 --> 39:18.731
Where was it, though?
I was looking all over.

39:18.814 --> 39:21.817
Oh, yes. It was buried down in storage.

39:22.902 --> 39:24.111
"Storage"?

39:24.195 --> 39:26.405
Checkout is over there. Thank you.

39:26.489 --> 39:27.490
[Tae-kyung] Thanks.

39:30.701 --> 39:33.579
CITY ALLIGATOR
BY JIN TAE-KYUNG

39:38.292 --> 39:40.836
[pensive music]

39:48.761 --> 39:49.678
[Seok-ho sighs]

39:59.313 --> 40:01.732
[playful music]

40:05.277 --> 40:06.153
[chuckles]

40:11.826 --> 40:13.202
[snickers]

40:18.332 --> 40:20.835
- Looking for this one?
- No, no. Go ahead.

40:24.797 --> 40:25.714
[inhales deeply]

40:26.715 --> 40:27.633
Aren't you…

40:30.678 --> 40:33.222
Oh, you recognize me?

40:34.473 --> 40:36.809
Well, oh, yes, I did…

40:37.935 --> 40:39.311
The side dish girl, right?

40:39.812 --> 40:41.313
"Side dishes"?

40:42.273 --> 40:46.152
You gave me those side dishes
to keep for your sister, Ms. 1201.

40:46.235 --> 40:47.319
Oh…

40:47.403 --> 40:48.946
Mr. 1302?

40:51.991 --> 40:54.827
[sighs]
Why hasn't she gone to get them? It's…

40:54.910 --> 40:57.163
[line ringing]

40:58.080 --> 40:59.915
She's not answering her phone.

41:04.378 --> 41:05.296
[sighs]

41:07.131 --> 41:09.842
Please tell your sister
that I'm going to throw

41:09.925 --> 41:12.928
every last one of them away
if she doesn't get them by tomorrow.

41:14.096 --> 41:15.181
Oh, just wait a second.

41:16.390 --> 41:17.600
You can't go yet.

41:18.976 --> 41:19.894
Why?

41:20.478 --> 41:24.148
Uh, that book you were reading,
City Alligator,

41:24.231 --> 41:28.444
please tell me which part made you laugh
like you were laughing.

41:28.527 --> 41:29.528
Ah…

41:30.654 --> 41:33.199
I didn't laugh because it was funny.

41:33.282 --> 41:34.492
Why, then?

41:35.701 --> 41:37.453
I just had the thought that the only way

41:37.536 --> 41:39.872
an alligator goes to
a city is if it's a purse.

41:40.956 --> 41:42.374
I mean, they're reptiles, right?

41:42.458 --> 41:43.417
They live in water.

41:43.501 --> 41:46.212
So it's not exactly like
they can just go and live in the city.

41:46.295 --> 41:48.297
Yet the book was called City Alligator.

41:48.380 --> 41:52.051
[scoffs]
Couldn't one call that poetic license?

41:53.719 --> 41:55.054
Let me tell you something.

41:55.137 --> 41:56.847
The person who wrote that book,

41:56.931 --> 41:59.099
I doubt they even looked up
alligators online.

41:59.183 --> 42:01.727
Let alone do any serious research
on the subject.

42:01.810 --> 42:02.937
I don't think that's true.

42:03.020 --> 42:04.355
If they did, they would have known

42:04.438 --> 42:07.399
that the toes on an alligator's hind feet
and forefeet are different.

42:08.567 --> 42:09.693
Toes on their…

42:10.277 --> 42:14.448
The thing about alligators is they
all have five toes on their front feet

42:14.532 --> 42:15.908
and in the back, just four.

42:16.742 --> 42:18.160
But in that book…
[Seok-ho chuckles]

42:19.203 --> 42:21.121
[sighs]
Jeez, well…

42:21.205 --> 42:22.081
[giggles]

42:22.164 --> 42:25.501
It's really true these days that writer
just means you picked up a pen.

42:25.584 --> 42:27.878
Still, that author lacked even the basics.

42:27.962 --> 42:29.964
I was laughing
'cause I thought it was sad.

42:30.047 --> 42:31.048
[laughs]

42:32.508 --> 42:35.219
- I'm sorry I lack the basics.
- Huh?

42:40.266 --> 42:42.476
Are you actually…

42:45.062 --> 42:47.231
[quirky music]

42:47.314 --> 42:48.232
Uh…

42:50.859 --> 42:51.944
[sighs]

42:58.492 --> 42:59.618
[chuckles]

43:01.078 --> 43:03.247
- This is done too.
- Thank you.

43:10.421 --> 43:11.797
[phone vibrates]

43:18.262 --> 43:19.138
[clanks]

43:22.474 --> 43:23.434
Who is it?

43:23.517 --> 43:25.644
Hmm. Oh, it's no one.

43:26.854 --> 43:27.980
[Si-woo] Is it good?

43:36.780 --> 43:38.741
Did I come on too strong earlier?

43:38.824 --> 43:39.867
What… what do you mean?

43:41.118 --> 43:42.244
Mm…

43:42.911 --> 43:45.039
I thought that
when I said we should move in,

43:45.122 --> 43:46.373
maybe that was too much.

43:47.708 --> 43:50.586
No. I like that you were being honest.

43:50.669 --> 43:53.464
It made me wanna tell you
my honest opinion as well.

43:55.716 --> 43:59.678
I feel like it's been a little awkward,
now that I brought it up.

43:59.762 --> 44:02.598
I felt like there's sort of a distance
between the two of us.

44:04.141 --> 44:07.144
Isn't that distance what you wanted?

44:07.227 --> 44:08.687
I mean to keep us a secret?

44:08.771 --> 44:11.607
Obviously, I didn't mean
to keep secrets from each other.

44:13.901 --> 44:17.529
Is this 'cause I didn't tell you
who that text was from?

44:19.031 --> 44:20.949
Mm, well, that's part of it. Mm-hmm.

44:22.326 --> 44:23.535
[chuckles]

44:25.913 --> 44:26.872
[grunts]

44:28.540 --> 44:29.583
Then here.

44:32.378 --> 44:33.337
A realtor?

44:33.837 --> 44:35.673
Yeah, a realtor.

44:35.756 --> 44:36.924
And the new tour.

44:37.508 --> 44:38.592
What is this for?

44:38.676 --> 44:40.678
I can't stay
at the training center forever.

44:42.054 --> 44:42.888
[Si-woo sighs]

44:42.971 --> 44:45.683
I knew that it's hard
to find a place in Seoul,

44:45.766 --> 44:47.518
but it's even harder than I thought.

44:48.102 --> 44:51.146
Yesterday, I was running around
all day, all for nothing.

44:52.106 --> 44:54.191
Is, um… Is this what you meant

44:54.274 --> 44:56.110
when you said
you had something to do yesterday?

44:56.193 --> 44:57.194
Yeah.

44:59.321 --> 45:02.074
Si-woo, I'm asking
because I'm genuinely curious.

45:02.157 --> 45:05.119
Why are you going
out of your way to do this

45:05.202 --> 45:07.329
when it would be so much easier
to move in with me?

45:08.288 --> 45:09.581
Mm, it's because

45:10.332 --> 45:14.086
I believe someone should keep
their love and private lives separate.

45:18.799 --> 45:20.634
Are you sure it's not about your ego?

45:23.679 --> 45:26.849
Director, I can't be honest with you
if you try to get under my skin.

45:28.267 --> 45:31.228
Honestly, I'm not proud
of my current situation, okay?

45:31.854 --> 45:34.314
But I'm not ashamed of it either.

45:37.025 --> 45:38.026
[light chuckle]

45:39.111 --> 45:41.029
What? What are you…

45:42.156 --> 45:43.532
It's nothing.

45:49.913 --> 45:51.957
- Enjoy.
- Thank you.

45:53.584 --> 45:55.294
Can we also have one bottle of soju?

45:55.377 --> 45:56.462
Yes.

46:07.264 --> 46:10.184
[quirky music]

46:23.322 --> 46:25.574
- What are you doing?
- Goddamn it!

46:25.657 --> 46:26.492
[groans]

46:27.493 --> 46:28.619
[Tae-kyung whines]

46:32.414 --> 46:33.874
I just asked.

46:33.957 --> 46:35.042
[coughs]

46:35.834 --> 46:36.793
Damn it.

46:37.711 --> 46:39.880
Ah!
[sobs]

46:41.715 --> 46:43.425
[knife chopping]

46:47.846 --> 46:48.889
Uh, what are…

46:50.724 --> 46:52.809
Are you hungry? Go and sit.

46:59.733 --> 47:01.818
[inhales]
Thank you for this.

47:02.569 --> 47:03.570
Mm-hmm.

47:20.712 --> 47:21.588
Uh, what's this?

47:21.672 --> 47:23.423
CREDIT LOANS
FOR FULL-TIME CIVIL SERVANTS

47:23.507 --> 47:25.884
Well, I thought we could pay
our deposit with a loan.

47:25.968 --> 47:28.011
Of course, this also puts us in debt.

47:28.095 --> 47:32.099
But the interest on this one is way better
than a home loan if you're newlyweds.

47:42.150 --> 47:45.237
I heard that your chief editor
asked if I could write a column.

47:45.320 --> 47:46.488
Where did you hear that?

47:47.155 --> 47:49.658
You really should have told me
about something like that.

47:51.410 --> 47:52.828
I know you're real busy.

47:53.537 --> 47:56.582
I just really didn't want
to add to your stress.

47:57.666 --> 47:59.960
Tell him your oppa is gonna do it.

48:01.336 --> 48:02.170
Serious?

48:02.254 --> 48:03.505
Mm-hmm.

48:03.589 --> 48:07.884
If I don't do it, then your chief editor
is gonna give you a hard time about it.

48:07.968 --> 48:10.846
And people will think that you can't get
your husband to do anything.

48:10.929 --> 48:12.472
Are you sure you have time, though?

48:13.265 --> 48:15.267
I'll do it even if I don't have the time.

48:15.350 --> 48:17.060
You're my wife, after all.

48:18.270 --> 48:21.064
Okay, but serious,
I'm gonna tell him tomorrow, okay?

48:21.148 --> 48:22.441
Yeah, go ahead.

48:23.984 --> 48:25.110
[both chuckle]

48:27.863 --> 48:29.573
By the way,
how did you find out about this?

48:30.824 --> 48:32.159
You're incredible.

48:32.743 --> 48:33.827
[giggles]

48:35.579 --> 48:37.497
[Myung-ju] Love is trusting together.

48:37.581 --> 48:41.543
They say that where there's trust,
courage will appear also.

48:42.127 --> 48:46.381
The courage to go through anything
if it's along with the one you love, okay?

48:52.638 --> 48:53.764
[both giggle]

48:54.848 --> 48:56.933
- [Hyang-rae] Did you do your homework?
- [student] Yes.

48:58.143 --> 49:01.188
Mm, then today, addition of involutions.

49:02.022 --> 49:04.274
- Try to solve this and this first.
- Okay.

49:10.197 --> 49:11.865
[giggling]

49:14.868 --> 49:18.538
What did you… mean
by what you said earlier?

49:19.122 --> 49:20.374
Hmm?

49:20.457 --> 49:23.627
Why would you say
I could divorce Dad if I want?

49:24.211 --> 49:25.170
You know.

49:26.713 --> 49:29.841
It seems like it's harder for you now
than it was when he was away.

49:30.467 --> 49:32.427
I just don't want you
going through that for me.

49:32.928 --> 49:34.429
I'm happy to live with Dad,

49:34.513 --> 49:36.890
but it's more important
to me that you are.

49:38.433 --> 49:41.436
No, I… I don't hate living with him.

49:42.312 --> 49:45.023
It's just… right now,

49:46.066 --> 49:48.360
your Pop and I just need
a little time alone.

49:48.944 --> 49:51.488
We've been apart for so long that…

49:52.781 --> 49:54.991
of course, we need
some time getting closer.

50:01.957 --> 50:02.916
[sighs]

50:06.545 --> 50:08.296
Okay. I've finished, Ms. Lee.

50:09.923 --> 50:11.049
Ms. Lee?

50:11.133 --> 50:13.051
- Huh?
- Can you take a look at this?

50:13.802 --> 50:15.804
Oh, okay. Let's see.

50:17.931 --> 50:20.559
[crickets chirping]

50:21.977 --> 50:23.395
[stomach rumbles]

50:25.689 --> 50:26.940
[grunts]

50:31.111 --> 50:32.112
[sighs]

50:38.285 --> 50:39.369
[grumbles]

50:46.001 --> 50:47.294
Dang it.
[groans]

50:51.965 --> 50:53.633
- [sighs]
- [door opens]

50:55.302 --> 50:56.845
FRIED CHICKEN

50:56.928 --> 50:58.138
[chuckles]

50:58.221 --> 50:59.264
[clacks]

51:00.682 --> 51:02.392
- [Si-woo] Here you go.
- Mm.

51:04.352 --> 51:06.313
Did you already have a drink somewhere?

51:06.396 --> 51:07.898
Yes, with my girlfriend.

51:08.607 --> 51:09.775
Just one.

51:09.858 --> 51:11.026
[sighs]

51:11.109 --> 51:14.529
Why did you come here
and not to her place, then, huh?

51:15.197 --> 51:16.490
[exhales]
I, uh…

51:17.616 --> 51:20.243
I'm a little… I'm a little embarrassed.

51:20.952 --> 51:21.870
Why?

51:21.953 --> 51:25.707
To be honest, I don't have
a penny in the world.

51:25.791 --> 51:27.459
I've been holding out…

51:27.542 --> 51:30.796
with the one thing I do have,
and that's my pride.

51:33.089 --> 51:34.549
Well, I got busted tonight.

51:37.469 --> 51:39.888
[wistful music]

51:43.767 --> 51:45.268
[Ha-kyung] Let me tell you a story.

51:47.938 --> 51:49.731
After my dad passed away,

51:51.733 --> 51:54.528
we were left with nothing,
not even a place to live.

51:57.531 --> 51:59.783
It was me, my sister, and my mom.

52:00.909 --> 52:03.703
The three of us had nowhere to go.

52:04.955 --> 52:07.958
We were hungry and it was so cold.

52:08.458 --> 52:10.877
Thinking that we might
have to stay outside all night,

52:11.378 --> 52:13.672
I just wanted to knock
on literally any door

52:13.755 --> 52:15.507
and ask if they could just let us stay.

52:15.590 --> 52:19.177
So, uh, what happened that night, then?

52:20.679 --> 52:22.264
We slept in the cold.

52:24.641 --> 52:27.602
The next day, my sister
went to live with my dad's older brother,

52:28.562 --> 52:30.856
and then I went
to my mom's younger sister.

52:30.939 --> 52:31.982
And Mom…

52:33.191 --> 52:34.734
got a job at a restaurant.

52:35.402 --> 52:37.612
So we had to live apart for a few years.

52:40.907 --> 52:44.744
So I understand what it's like
to have nowhere to go.

52:45.328 --> 52:48.123
And I also know how weary
your heart is right now.

52:50.625 --> 52:54.296
I respect you wanting to keep a line
between your love and your private life.

52:56.673 --> 52:58.174
And I also respect your pride

52:58.258 --> 53:00.260
and not wanting
to be embarrassed over all this.

53:01.636 --> 53:03.388
But I just want you to know…

53:05.765 --> 53:08.435
you don't have to try too hard
to act like you're okay.

53:13.106 --> 53:14.149
Okay?

53:19.738 --> 53:23.825
Oh, it's always so embarrassing
to be called out on your bluff, huh?

53:25.201 --> 53:27.829
Yeah, well… that's true.

53:28.413 --> 53:32.208
However, believe it or not,
I'm really relieved now.

53:34.711 --> 53:36.588
I feel like at least with this woman,

53:36.671 --> 53:40.634
I won't have to pretend
like everything's okay when it's not.

53:41.843 --> 53:45.805
I don't think it'll hurt,
even when I get closer to her.

53:45.889 --> 53:47.015
[chuckles]

53:48.350 --> 53:49.225
Right.

53:49.309 --> 53:51.853
Her. That's when you know
the right distance.

53:54.356 --> 53:57.317
"The right distance."

54:00.946 --> 54:02.781
- [clacks]
- Oh, I'm full.

54:04.824 --> 54:06.743
Let's wrap it up now, eh? Enough chitchat.

54:08.453 --> 54:09.287
Sorry?

54:10.288 --> 54:12.582
Let's rest. We have work tomorrow.

54:14.376 --> 54:16.127
Wait, you're saying I can sleep here?

54:16.211 --> 54:18.046
Who am I to say yes or no to that?

54:18.630 --> 54:20.674
Oh, and I snore at night.

54:21.257 --> 54:23.426
Oh, come on. That stuff's no problem.

54:23.510 --> 54:24.761
[chuckles]

54:24.844 --> 54:26.096
[laughs]

54:27.180 --> 54:29.432
[Dong-han snoring loudly]

54:30.433 --> 54:31.685
[Si-woo sighs]

54:33.019 --> 54:34.688
[loud snoring]

54:38.984 --> 54:40.318
[Si-woo groans]

54:43.071 --> 54:46.574
[loud snoring]

54:48.451 --> 54:52.288
[snoring continues]

55:06.428 --> 55:07.595
[engine stops]

55:13.810 --> 55:14.728
[door locks]

55:19.649 --> 55:23.028
I already submitted the response
about the Ms. Kim situation.

55:23.111 --> 55:24.738
Oh, uh…
[chuckles]

55:25.822 --> 55:26.948
[Ki-jun] Here, have this.

55:28.408 --> 55:30.493
- What's going on?
- Here.

55:33.455 --> 55:37.751
Uh, well, actually, you know
the chief editor of Munmin Daily?

55:38.460 --> 55:41.212
He read my column and, uh, he liked it.

55:41.296 --> 55:44.049
Now he wants me to write a feature article
for the newspaper next week.

55:44.132 --> 55:46.051
A feature article on weather.

55:46.968 --> 55:47.886
Okay, so?

55:48.678 --> 55:51.890
I was wondering if you were free to…

55:52.515 --> 55:54.559
I told you with the last one
that we were through.

55:54.642 --> 55:56.603
[sighs]
Just… just this once, Ha-kyung.

55:56.686 --> 55:58.313
I already told them that I'd do it.

55:58.897 --> 56:00.148
Okay, and so?

56:00.231 --> 56:02.942
All you have to do is just read it over
before I submit it.

56:03.026 --> 56:04.319
This is really the last time.

56:04.402 --> 56:06.154
Just one more time. Please, Ha-kyung.

56:06.237 --> 56:09.908
Hey. Does your wife know that you're
asking for all this stuff right now?

56:09.991 --> 56:12.410
What, uh… How could I tell her?

56:12.494 --> 56:14.079
You can't because
you're humiliated, right?

56:14.162 --> 56:15.580
Have a shred of that with me.

56:16.414 --> 56:17.415
Jin Ha-kyung.

56:18.458 --> 56:19.667
Hey, we're friends.

56:20.460 --> 56:21.419
Seriously?

56:21.503 --> 56:23.630
You and I have known each other
for ten years.

56:23.713 --> 56:25.840
We failed as lovers,
but doesn't our friendship remain?

56:25.924 --> 56:27.592
We spent so much time together
since college.

56:27.675 --> 56:30.929
The love is gone, but all
the other good memories are still there.

56:31.012 --> 56:33.181
- Don't you see that?
- No, I do not.

56:33.264 --> 56:35.767
I already forgot all my time
with you, Han Ki-jun.

56:35.850 --> 56:36.893
I feel nothing for you.

56:36.976 --> 56:38.311
Ha-kyung, hey.

56:39.020 --> 56:42.315
If you ask me about this anymore,
your wife's gonna hear about it.

56:45.485 --> 56:47.946
Jin Ha-kyung, how could you do this, huh?

56:48.530 --> 56:49.447
Ha-kyung!

56:50.281 --> 56:51.574
Director!

56:52.742 --> 56:55.161
[sighs]
What will I do?

56:55.787 --> 56:57.539
[sighs]
Oh…

56:59.040 --> 56:59.916
[groans]

57:05.004 --> 57:07.006
Good morning. The night watch is over.

57:07.590 --> 57:09.509
You're always a sunny spirit,
aren't you, Director?

57:10.093 --> 57:11.427
Oh, well, thanks.

57:11.511 --> 57:13.805
But I think there's something
that you should know about your team.

57:13.888 --> 57:16.224
Yes, there is a situation
going on with your teammates.

57:16.307 --> 57:17.517
My teammates?

57:18.184 --> 57:20.645
Haven't you heard,
they're living in the night-duty room?

57:20.728 --> 57:22.605
Oh, Mr. Um, yes.

57:22.689 --> 57:25.316
Forgive his situation.
He won't be there for too long.

57:26.025 --> 57:27.861
Everyone has a situation
around this place.

57:27.944 --> 57:29.946
One person alone hogging the bed is bad.

57:30.029 --> 57:32.740
But with two, where can
the night-duty team go?

57:34.993 --> 57:37.287
Did you just say "two"?

57:37.787 --> 57:41.374
[suspenseful music]

57:41.958 --> 57:44.085
[Young-gil] Managing your teammates
is part of your job.

57:44.586 --> 57:46.838
Do you think Director Choi
would have let this happen?

57:48.006 --> 57:49.466
[knocks on door]

57:49.549 --> 57:51.301
- [Ha-kyung] Lee Si-woo--
- [Dong-han gasps]

57:55.763 --> 57:57.599
- Oh…
- Um…

58:03.271 --> 58:04.898
Why are you two doing this?

58:05.482 --> 58:09.277
If you really don't have anywhere to stay,
go to a motel or a jjimjilbang.

58:09.360 --> 58:11.863
Well, you see, I have to come
to work early anyway,

58:11.946 --> 58:13.323
so I just need a place to sleep.

58:15.158 --> 58:16.659
It's weird to go
to a jjimjilbang in summer.

58:21.122 --> 58:22.665
Why are you not at the training center?

58:22.749 --> 58:25.418
Wasn't that where you were staying
during your apartment hunt?

58:26.044 --> 58:27.212
Well, that's--

58:27.295 --> 58:28.922
He got kicked out of there

58:29.005 --> 58:30.215
a few days ago.

58:31.925 --> 58:33.343
"A few days ago"?

58:33.927 --> 58:36.679
You're saying you've been staying
for a few days in the night-duty room?

58:36.763 --> 58:39.516
- Uh…
- No. He's only been here for two days.

58:39.599 --> 58:40.850
Before that, he was in his car.

58:40.934 --> 58:42.268
[utensils clank]

58:42.352 --> 58:44.270
Hey, what the heck's wrong
with you, huh, man?

58:44.354 --> 58:45.522
Why would you tell…

58:47.732 --> 58:48.858
Wow.

58:50.193 --> 58:52.946
You know what, we're really okay.

58:53.446 --> 58:55.949
We'll take care of it,
and you don't have to worry at all.

58:56.032 --> 58:58.493
How could I not worry? How though?

58:58.576 --> 59:01.371
Everyone's coming to me 'cause they're mad
that you two are living down there.

59:01.955 --> 59:03.706
Why not say it directly to our faces?

59:03.790 --> 59:04.832
What are they saying?

59:04.916 --> 59:06.751
That I'm delinquent as a leader.

59:06.834 --> 59:09.295
They're asking how long
I'll neglect you two.

59:10.755 --> 59:11.756
Ah.

59:13.841 --> 59:15.593
[Dong-han slurping]

59:15.677 --> 59:17.845
[quirky music]

59:21.140 --> 59:22.058
[sighs]

59:22.767 --> 59:24.894
- What to do?
- [door opens]

59:24.978 --> 59:28.064
- [Ju-won] Hey, Han Ki-jun.
- [door closes]

59:28.731 --> 59:30.984
I heard you're writing
that feature for Munmin Daily.

59:32.193 --> 59:34.320
Uh, um…

59:34.404 --> 59:36.114
[Ki-jun] Yes. Yeah.

59:36.990 --> 59:40.368
I knew it. Your wife's power over you
is greater than mine.

59:41.202 --> 59:44.372
You were talking up and down about
how you'd never do it yesterday, huh?

59:44.455 --> 59:46.874
Of course, when your wife asks,
"Of course, ma'am, I will."

59:46.958 --> 59:49.794
[chuckles]
I wouldn't say it quite like that.

59:50.503 --> 59:53.131
Wow, a sacrifice for love. Godspeed.

59:54.299 --> 59:55.758
- And good luck.
- Thanks.

59:57.635 --> 59:58.553
That's really nice.

59:59.178 --> 01:00:00.179
[clonks]

01:00:00.263 --> 01:00:02.432
- Good luck.
- Way to go!

01:00:02.515 --> 01:00:06.060
Okay. Let's go!
[laughs awkwardly]

01:00:07.478 --> 01:00:08.771
[groans]

01:00:11.566 --> 01:00:13.026
[softly]
What do I do?

01:00:13.109 --> 01:00:15.111
[clanking]

01:00:18.448 --> 01:00:19.490
[pops]

01:00:24.996 --> 01:00:25.955
[sighs]

01:00:29.167 --> 01:00:30.710
Do I really have to do this?

01:00:33.588 --> 01:00:35.715
[groans]
Yes, I do.

01:00:36.299 --> 01:00:38.092
Hmm. Let's do it.

01:00:39.552 --> 01:00:43.473
[woman 1] Reporter Chae Yu-jin's writing
got better after she got married.

01:00:44.724 --> 01:00:46.893
The title is really on point, too.

01:00:47.393 --> 01:00:49.812
[woman 2] Her husband works
at the KMA, you know.

01:00:50.647 --> 01:00:55.985
I heard a rumor that she was living
with a KMA employee before.

01:00:56.069 --> 01:00:59.238
I guess she ended up marrying that guy.

01:01:00.448 --> 01:01:02.617
Uh-huh. I heard that too.

01:01:03.493 --> 01:01:06.913
- Mm-hmm.
- I heard her husband's a good writer, huh?

01:01:08.915 --> 01:01:11.459
- [woman 1] Ooh!
- She really does have it all, doesn't she?

01:01:11.542 --> 01:01:13.878
[woman 1] Getting married
after living together?

01:01:14.587 --> 01:01:16.005
[woman 2] That's the right move.

01:01:16.089 --> 01:01:19.175
[woman 1] Oh, by the way, do you know
which division her husband's in?

01:01:19.258 --> 01:01:21.094
[unsettling music]

01:01:21.177 --> 01:01:26.432
INNOVATIVE WEATHER SERVICES
A STEPPING STONE TO PUBLIC SAFETY

01:01:29.185 --> 01:01:33.356
I don't know about Forecaster Lee
but Mr. Um can go back to his family.

01:01:33.439 --> 01:01:34.357
[Seok-ho] Yeah.

01:01:34.899 --> 01:01:36.359
I wish I could just take him home.

01:01:36.442 --> 01:01:38.236
That, uh, would be hard with two kids.

01:01:38.861 --> 01:01:39.779
With three.

01:01:39.862 --> 01:01:41.698
'Cause my husband's beginning
a year of absence.

01:01:41.781 --> 01:01:42.740
Ah.

01:01:42.824 --> 01:01:43.991
Why not at your place?

01:01:44.575 --> 01:01:46.035
I think I'll be going now. Bye.

01:01:49.163 --> 01:01:50.915
It's not going to happen.

01:01:50.998 --> 01:01:53.501
The Assistant Director is so fastidious,
he never would.

01:01:53.584 --> 01:01:57.505
Well, I'm sorry for Director Jin
having this situation.

01:01:57.588 --> 01:01:59.674
[Soo-jin sighs]
I know.

01:02:05.096 --> 01:02:07.098
Ah, darn. This is still wet.

01:02:08.015 --> 01:02:09.016
[sighs]

01:02:09.517 --> 01:02:10.935
What's car sleeping like?

01:02:11.018 --> 01:02:16.524
Well, except for the mosquito bites
and the neck cramps, it's not that rough.

01:02:17.191 --> 01:02:19.986
Ah, damn it. I hate mosquitoes.

01:02:20.653 --> 01:02:23.865
[mosquito buzzing]

01:02:30.496 --> 01:02:31.706
[sighs]

01:02:32.749 --> 01:02:34.751
[mosquito buzzing]

01:02:37.587 --> 01:02:38.504
[grunts]

01:02:39.714 --> 01:02:40.757
[chuckles]

01:02:43.885 --> 01:02:47.221
How am I supposed to sleep in here? Oh.

01:02:50.975 --> 01:02:51.809
[grunts]

01:02:55.980 --> 01:02:58.524
[comical music]

01:03:00.610 --> 01:03:02.779
[chuckles]

01:03:25.426 --> 01:03:26.844
Come in. What are you doing?

01:03:27.428 --> 01:03:28.763
- Oh…
- Okay.

01:03:31.390 --> 01:03:34.268
Mr. Um can take the study
along with your suitcase.

01:03:34.352 --> 01:03:35.603
And Mr. Lee will go there.

01:03:37.980 --> 01:03:39.982
[Dong-han sighs]
It's really okay for us to stay?

01:03:40.066 --> 01:03:41.359
You're not here free of charge.

01:03:41.442 --> 01:03:44.612
I'm going to ask each of you
for a third of the utility fee.

01:03:44.695 --> 01:03:46.447
Hmm, one-third, huh?

01:03:47.198 --> 01:03:49.992
If you two don't like that,
then Mr. Um can go back home,

01:03:50.076 --> 01:03:51.744
and Mr. Lee can find a place of his own.

01:03:51.828 --> 01:03:54.038
Shouldn't we just stay at a motel, huh?

01:03:55.456 --> 01:03:57.333
Or maybe a jjimjilbang?

01:03:57.416 --> 01:04:00.670
Oh, yeah. That's more comfortable
than here, right?

01:04:00.753 --> 01:04:02.171
Uh, we'll be on our way, then.

01:04:02.672 --> 01:04:05.132
Is there some kind of tension with me?

01:04:05.216 --> 01:04:06.592
Hey, don't joke about that.

01:04:06.676 --> 01:04:09.887
Hey, no, that's ridiculous.
[chuckles]

01:04:09.971 --> 01:04:11.931
If it's not that, you should stay.

01:04:12.014 --> 01:04:14.892
The pretext can be
the top minds of our team

01:04:14.976 --> 01:04:17.687
have formed a summer camp
for monsoon season.

01:04:17.770 --> 01:04:19.897
"Top minds"? So, even me?

01:04:19.981 --> 01:04:22.692
I think, for this one,
that's a little generous.

01:04:22.775 --> 01:04:24.569
Hey, no. Come on, eh. Don't you remember?

01:04:24.652 --> 01:04:27.363
I predicted the hailstorm
over the city back in March.

01:04:27.446 --> 01:04:29.282
That was luck, okay?

01:04:29.365 --> 01:04:30.741
Sheer beginner's luck, that's all.

01:04:30.825 --> 01:04:32.743
Don't forget I predicted
the rainstorms too.

01:04:33.327 --> 01:04:35.204
I think you two
are gonna drive me to drink.

01:04:37.290 --> 01:04:39.500
Uh, so I should grab some cold beers?

01:04:39.584 --> 01:04:41.794
Snacks too, okay?
Some dried squid or something?

01:04:41.878 --> 01:04:43.129
- Uh, yeah. For sure.
- Right.

01:04:43.212 --> 01:04:45.172
- I'll be back soon, okay?
- Uh-huh.

01:04:47.008 --> 01:04:47.925
Uh…

01:04:48.801 --> 01:04:49.886
The bathroom, huh?

01:04:49.969 --> 01:04:52.138
- Uh, right over there.
- [door lock chiming]

01:04:52.221 --> 01:04:54.849
I'll use the master bathroom,
so that one's yours.

01:04:54.932 --> 01:04:56.726
Oh, thanks.

01:04:58.853 --> 01:04:59.979
Hey, uh…

01:05:00.730 --> 01:05:04.150
I'm sorry for the imposition, really.

01:05:04.233 --> 01:05:06.652
I'll find a place as soon as possible.

01:05:06.736 --> 01:05:07.653
Okay.

01:05:12.366 --> 01:05:13.576
[Seok-ho inhales heavily]

01:05:13.659 --> 01:05:15.328
[exhales sharply]

01:05:18.497 --> 01:05:19.332
[fridge door closes]

01:05:21.667 --> 01:05:23.502
Uh…

01:05:23.586 --> 01:05:26.547
What kind of beer would Mr. Um want?

01:05:29.300 --> 01:05:30.676
[chuckles]

01:05:39.602 --> 01:05:41.228
[footsteps shuffling]

01:05:42.396 --> 01:05:44.815
[quirky music]

01:05:48.611 --> 01:05:50.154
[door lock chimes]

01:06:01.832 --> 01:06:03.000
[sighs]

01:06:06.629 --> 01:06:08.089
[elevator dings]

01:06:09.632 --> 01:06:10.800
Oh!

01:06:13.928 --> 01:06:16.681
[upbeat music]

01:06:19.308 --> 01:06:21.644
Oh, food girl! It's food girl.

01:06:22.853 --> 01:06:25.022
[breathing heavily]

01:06:30.903 --> 01:06:32.405
[doorbell rings]

01:06:33.406 --> 01:06:35.032
He should remember the code.

01:06:37.827 --> 01:06:38.953
That was quick.

01:06:40.871 --> 01:06:41.998
Ha-kyung.

01:06:43.332 --> 01:06:44.750
What are you doing here?

01:06:45.376 --> 01:06:47.294
[Ki-jun] I knew it. You were here.

01:06:47.878 --> 01:06:49.755
I had a feeling this was your home, huh?

01:06:49.839 --> 01:06:52.758
Who cares what you were thinking?
What do you want?

01:06:52.842 --> 01:06:54.218
It's just that…

01:06:55.678 --> 01:06:58.139
- I thought of you.
- What?

01:06:58.222 --> 01:07:00.391
Can I come in for a second?

01:07:00.474 --> 01:07:01.851
Are you crazy?

01:07:01.934 --> 01:07:04.895
[huffs]
How did you know how I feel?

01:07:04.979 --> 01:07:08.149
I feel like I am going crazy.
[sucks teeth]

01:07:08.232 --> 01:07:11.485
I'm so tired.
Can I please just come inside?

01:07:11.569 --> 01:07:15.281
Ugh! Go home and tell your wife
about it, okay, man?

01:07:15.364 --> 01:07:16.782
[grunts]

01:07:16.866 --> 01:07:20.536
I have something to say to you.
Just let me in. Let me in!

01:07:20.619 --> 01:07:22.371
You're not coming any closer!

01:07:22.455 --> 01:07:24.040
Is someone here?

01:07:25.624 --> 01:07:27.043
Who else is here?

01:07:28.127 --> 01:07:29.837
It's none of your concern. Just go back…

01:07:29.920 --> 01:07:32.131
- [Ha-kyung] Uh-uh-uh…
- I hear a male voice.

01:07:32.214 --> 01:07:34.258
- Who is it, huh?
- Hey!

01:07:39.180 --> 01:07:43.059
[groans]
I think I'm pretty drunk, man.

01:07:43.559 --> 01:07:45.061
Why are you here at this hour?

01:07:46.187 --> 01:07:49.607
Huh? Is that Mr. Um?
What is he doing here?

01:07:52.860 --> 01:07:54.403
Director Jin?

01:07:54.987 --> 01:07:56.363
Assistant Director Shin?

01:07:56.947 --> 01:07:58.365
Oh, Mr. Shin.

01:07:58.449 --> 01:08:00.451
How come you're here, Senior Forecaster?

01:08:01.077 --> 01:08:03.746
Well, because Director Jin told me
I could stay here with her.

01:08:03.829 --> 01:08:06.415
Oh, stay here with her?

01:08:06.999 --> 01:08:08.167
Oh…

01:08:08.250 --> 01:08:09.251
Uh…

01:08:09.919 --> 01:08:13.422
Uh, Director Jin, are you saying
this is your apartment?

01:08:14.507 --> 01:08:15.758
Yes, it is.

01:08:15.841 --> 01:08:17.510
Why are you here, Assistant Director?

01:08:17.593 --> 01:08:20.012
I live upstairs, 1302.

01:08:20.763 --> 01:08:21.680
Really?

01:08:22.306 --> 01:08:24.100
Uh, you two are neighbors, huh?

01:08:24.183 --> 01:08:27.144
Wait a minute. What's happening right now?

01:08:27.228 --> 01:08:29.313
Wait. Just wait a second.

01:08:29.814 --> 01:08:31.899
- [elevator dings]
- [automated voice] Doors opening.

01:08:36.237 --> 01:08:37.905
Oh, Seok-ho.

01:08:39.573 --> 01:08:41.450
[automated voice] Doors closing.

01:08:42.034 --> 01:08:42.868
You!

01:08:46.330 --> 01:08:47.915
Uh, what's going on here?

01:08:47.998 --> 01:08:49.500
That's what I want to know.

01:08:52.294 --> 01:08:54.713
Ha-kyung, what the hell's going on?

01:08:56.090 --> 01:08:56.966
[sighs]

01:08:57.049 --> 01:09:00.636
[Ha-kyung] The life is a sequence
of unexpected events.

01:09:05.683 --> 01:09:08.018
Why are all these people
in your apartment?

01:09:08.102 --> 01:09:09.770
Shut your mouth and just follow me.

01:09:09.854 --> 01:09:11.480
[grunting]

01:09:11.564 --> 01:09:13.107
- [Ha-kyung] How much more…
- Ha-kyung!

01:09:13.190 --> 01:09:17.444
…do we need to poke each other
before we figure out the optimal distance?

01:09:20.239 --> 01:09:23.075
["Promise You" by Kyuhyun playing]

01:09:43.846 --> 01:09:46.515
You burst into my home in the middle
of the night to cause drama? Why?

01:09:46.599 --> 01:09:48.100
It's all my fault, Ha-kyung.

01:09:49.602 --> 01:09:51.061
My love Ha-kyung was…

01:09:51.145 --> 01:09:53.063
Wake up! This isn't okay!

01:09:53.147 --> 01:09:56.400
I'm so sorry, Ha-kyung.

01:09:56.483 --> 01:09:57.484
[scoffs]

01:09:57.568 --> 01:10:01.822
[Si-woo] I like you more than anyone
I've known, and that's a little scary.

01:10:01.906 --> 01:10:04.200
How many reasons are there
for Han Ki-jun to see you?

01:10:04.283 --> 01:10:05.826
It seems endless.

01:10:07.036 --> 01:10:10.664
Well, can you guess
who in this building is her ex-boyfriend?

01:10:10.748 --> 01:10:13.918
[grunts]
This is all your fault!

01:10:14.001 --> 01:10:15.544
- [grunts]
- [thwacks]

01:10:15.628 --> 01:10:16.629
Damn!

01:10:16.712 --> 01:10:17.796
Lee Si-woo, quit it!

01:10:18.464 --> 01:10:21.467
["Promise You" by Kyuhyun
continues playing]
